ity at scale is to treat transparency as a computational problem, not a legal one. We must automate the internal auditing of model weights and latent spaces so that we can verify performance metrics in real-time, rather than relying on the paper-pushing of 'provenance manifests.' By focusing on the material reality of model performance through empirical, automated testing, we can accelerate the development of systems that are far more robust and verifiable than any human-documented dataset could ever be.",
